course: dictionary
lesson: 7578
title: Pretend: acting as if, or playing make-believe
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pretend is a verb that can mean two things. Often it means acting as if something is true when it is not. «The wolf pretended to be Grandma» means the wolf acted like Grandma to trick someone. Pretend can also mean a make-believe game: «Let's pretend we're pirates» means we make up a story and play it.
explain: Look at the words around pretend to find its meaning. Pretend to be, pretend that, let's pretend and pretend play are common phrases. If the sentence is about a trick or a lie, pretend means to fool someone. If it is about games, pretend means make-believe.
explain: Pretend can also be an informal adjective, as in «a pretend shop», which means not real. Children use pretend money when they play shops. To check, swap in your meaning: «a make-believe shop» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Pretending is not always bad. Pretend play helps your imagination, but pretending to be ill to miss school is lying, and pretending to be fouled in sport is cheating. Think about why someone is pretending before you decide what it means.
fact: Pretend means to act as if something is true when it is not, or to play a make-believe game.
fact: «Let's pretend we're pirates» means we are playing a make-believe game.
fact: «The wolf pretended to be Grandma» means the wolf acted like Grandma to fool someone.
fact: Pretend play, like playing shop or superheroes, helps children use their imagination.
fact: As an informal adjective, «pretend» means not real, make-believe, as in «a pretend shop».
exercise: «The wolf pretended to be Grandma.» What does pretended mean here? | Played a game of pirates | Ran away very fast | Gave Grandma a present | *Acted as if he was Grandma to trick someone
exercise: «Let's pretend we're pirates.» What does pretend mean here? | *Make-believe, playing a game | Pretending to be ill | Telling a lie to get out of trouble | Working very hard
exercise: Which word in «a pretend shop» means not real, make-believe? | *pretend | a | shop
test: «Pretending to be ill to miss school» is what kind of act? | *A form of lying | Sharing a snack | A helpful act | Playing a game
test: Your friend says, «Let's pretend the sofa is a boat.» What does your friend want? | To sell the sofa | To tell a lie about the boat | *To play a make-believe game | To sleep on the floor
exam: «Grown-ups can pretend to be children online» means what? | Children are always online playing games | Grown-ups should never use the internet | Grown-ups are always honest online | *Some grown-ups may act as if they are children to trick people
